prompts {'Thanks for your explanation, it will help me a lot.', 'Generate a markdown table of at least 20 English-Japanese flash cards for a beginner learning the Japanese language.', '- What areas of tech are you most interested in? \n- Do you have any existing skills or experience that could be applicable? \n- What is your learning style? \n- What is your current situation? \n- What are your goals and ideal job outcome?', 'What is a set in Python?', "Could you provide me with a proper cooking recipe? I think I'm missing some key ingredients and tips on how I can make this better and what are my options here?", 'Thank you for the valuable information and advice. I will definitely consider these steps as I work towards fixing my relationship. Communication, identifying the issue, compromise, seeking support, and practicing forgiveness are all important aspects to focus on. I appreciate your help and guidance.', 'I\'ve been learning Rust for a few weeks now, and have been trying my hand at the fizzbuzz problem.\n\nCode:\nfn fizzbuzz<\'a>(n: usize) -> &\'a str {\n\tmatch (n % 3, n % 5) {\n\t\t(0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",\n\t\t(0, _) => "fizz",\n\t\t(_, 0) => "buzz",\n\t\t_ => n.to_string().as_str(),\n\t}\n}\n\nFor some reason, I get a compiler error that I\'m struggling to understand.\n\nError:\nerror[E0515]: cannot return value referencing temporary value\n  --> src\\main.rs:36:2\n   |\n36 | /     match (n % 3, n % 5) {\n37 | |         (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",\n38 | |         (0, _) => "fizz",\n39 | |         (_, 0) => "buzz",\n40 | |         _ => n.to_string().as_str(),\n   | |              ------------- temporary value created here\n41 | |     }\n   | |_____^ returns a value referencing data owned by the current function\n\nFor more information about this error, try `rustc --explain E0515`.\n\nCould you please explain to my why this happens and how I can fix it?', 'What are some examples of songs that use this successfully', 'Can you please explain how Open Assistant works? I am specifically looking for a discussion of how the model is trained and what the model architecture is. Second, I would appreciate a description of the motives behind why Open Assistant was created.', 'Find and fix the errors in the following two sentences: "He wenting to the store and he buyed an apples. He then goed back home and ate a Apple with an very smile."', 'What is a dictionary in Python?', 'What is a string in Python?', 'So why does the sky appear orange-red in the evening as apposed to blue?', 'What is a variable in Python?', 'Can you give me the solutions to those problems?', "I'm trying to write a script that will take a string as input and return a list of all possible palindromes that can be formed using the characters in the string. Can you help me with the code?"}


